{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.SnapPyAxioms","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SnapPyAxioms","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SnapPyAxioms.snappy_L6a4_volume_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SnapPyAxioms.snappy_L6a4_volume_pos","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SnapPyAxioms.lean#L81-L88","doc":"The hyperbolic volume of L6a4 is positive.  **Theorem** (was\npreviously an axiom; discharged 2026-06-07).  Proof: `8 · G > 0`\nvia `catalan_G_pos`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SnapPyAxioms.snappy_L6a4_volume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SnapPyAxioms.snappy_L6a4_volume","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SnapPyAxioms.lean#L53-L79","doc":"Hyperbolic volume of the SnapPy manifold `L6a4` — the\nBorromean rings complement, denoted `𝓑₃` in the QOU framework.\n\nProducer witness:\n`computations/snappy-borromean-volume.witness.json`.\nRecords the canonical value (Adams 1985: `Vol(L6a4) = 8·G`\nwhere G is Catalan's constant) at multiple precision tiers\n(15 / 30 / 50 / 100 / 200 dps). Independent cross-check via\n`computations/borromean_volume_100dps.py`\n(Lobachevsky integration at 100 dps).\n\n**Definitional bridge** (2026-06-07).  The closed-form\ncharacterisation `snappy_L6a4_volume = 8·G` is the\n`vol_B3_eq_8_catalan` theorem in\n[`BorromeanVolumeCatalan.lean`](./BorromeanVolumeCatalan.lean);\nthat theorem was previously an axiom and is now closed by `rfl`\nafter `vol_B3` was redefined symbolically as `8 · catalan_G`.\nPer the file-level docstring's promise — *\"when that theorem\ncloses, this axiom becomes a named constant whose value is\n`8·G`\"* — `snappy_L6a4_volume` and its positivity are now\ndischarged here as `def` / `theorem` referencing the upstream\n`QOU.Archimedean.{catalan_G, catalan_G_pos}`.\n\n-- Ref: [culler2024] snappy-borromean-volume.witness.json\n-- Ref: [adams1985hyperbolic] Adams 1985, Proc. Amer. Math. Soc. 100, 601-606\n","signatureChunk":0}]}